WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:02.760
Hold onto your hats, true believers.

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:07.260
While Marvel Studios Phase 4 is pretty much
set in stone, and Phase 5 is only beginning

00:00:07.279 --> 00:00:11.760
to take shape, the rumor mill has churned
out an eye-popper: the studio is reportedly

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.760
prepping an ​Avengers vs. X-Men​ movie,
possibly for Phase 6.

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:19.680
The report comes from our friends at We Got
This Covered, who we know don't always nail

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.360
it when it comes to the Marvel pipeline.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.619
But that hasn't stopped them from making this
bold claim about the future of the MCU.

00:00:25.619 --> 00:00:29.740
Citing inside sources, the publication put
forth a surprising number of details about

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.090
the alleged Avengers vs. X-Men project.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.280
"Are you sure you saw what you saw?"

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.569
According to these sources the proposed picture
would come down the pike well after the X-Men

00:00:39.569 --> 00:00:44.020
have been introduced into the MCU, which is
not expected to happen for two years or more.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.890
It would involve different Avengers from the
ones that we all know and love, which squares

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:52.200
with comments made by Marvel head honcho Kevin
Feige to MTV News back in June.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.499
Feige said at the time,

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.520
"[The new Avengers] will be a very different
team than we've seen before; that's what Endgame

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:58.380
was all about.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.980
It will be a very different incarnation of
the team, with some people you've already

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:04.170
met, and some people you haven't met yet."

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:09.240
According to WGTC's sources, the team that
Marvel has in mind fits that description to

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.909
a T. Black Panther, Scarlet Witch, and assuming
that Sony and Marvel eventually get around

00:01:13.909 --> 00:01:17.960
to ironing out their differences Spider-Man
could all be on board, as well as the Jane

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:22.640
Foster version of Thor, who is set to make
her debut in 2022's Thor: Love and Thunder.

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:27.580
Also up for spots on the team: Simu Liu's
Shang-Chi, whose solo feature Shang-Chi and

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:32.979
the Legend of the Ten Rings drops in February
2021, and Mahershala Ali's Blade, whose solo

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:35.240
movie is thought to be scaring up Phase 5.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:39.060
Even more intriguingly, the flick is said
to be taking the inspiration for its plot

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:43.999
from a mind-blowing Marvel storyline: House
of M. The 2005 crossover event, penned by

00:01:43.999 --> 00:01:48.520
comics legend Brian Michael Bendis, mostly
took place in an alternate reality created

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:51.490
by Scarlet Witch after she suffered a mental
breakdown.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:57.159
But most notably, Wanda also used her reality-altering
abilities to depower virtually every mutant

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:57.740
on Earth.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:00.940
Not in the alternate reality, but in the actual
Marvel U.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.350
The events of House of M had a lasting effect
on the Marvel universe, and elements of the

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:10.500
story led into the 2012 Avengers vs. X-Men
crossover, also co-written by Bendis.

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:14.760
Obviously, a good number of tweaks would have
to be made to adapt the story to the screen,

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:18.680
but this is nothing new for Marvel; Captain
America: Civil War took a ton of liberties

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:23.880
with the 2006-2007 event from which it took
its title, just as the one-two punch of Avengers:

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:28.620
Infinity War and Avengers: Endgame did with
1991's Infinity Gauntlet limited series.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:32.700
While the news of a potential Avengers vs.
X-Men movie might sound like a whole lot of

00:02:32.709 --> 00:02:37.570
wishful thinking, it's worth mentioning that
the very same sources that supplied WGTC with

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:41.860
the intel have been right on the money with
their Marvel rumor-mongering on multiple occasions.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:45.520
They had previously leaked that the real Mandarin
would be the villain of Shang-Chi and the

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:49.569
Ten Rings, that the post-credits scene in
the Avengers: Endgame re-release would center

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:54.159
on the Hulk, and that iconic Marvel baddie
the Taskmaster would be the primary antagonist

00:02:54.159 --> 00:02:58.629
of next year's Black Widow; all of these reports
turned out to be accurate, so while they may

00:02:58.629 --> 00:03:02.840
be wrong sometimes, these folks do seem to
have managed to sneak a few top secret files

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.420
out of Marvel Studios' offices under their
trenchcoats.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:10.319
We may not yet know exactly how Mighty Marvel
will approach folding the X-Men into the MCU

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:14.970
or how its take will differ from the long-running
Fox Studios X-Men film series, but we're going

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:19.319
to go ahead and state the obvious: an Avengers
vs. X-Men flick has the potential to be nothing

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:20.260
short of epic.

00:03:20.569 --> 00:03:24.100
If we ever do get a formal announcement, the
force of fans' heads all around the world

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.440
exploding will register on the Richter scale.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:30.790
Obviously, Marvel loves to keep details about
its upcoming films and television series close

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.940
to the vest, meaning that even if Avengers
vs. X-Men is being actively developed, we're

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:38.580
not going to hear anything official about
it for a long, long time.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:42.220
"They can threaten me all they want, Charles.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.080
I'll never tell them where you are."

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:48.680
But you'd better believe that we'll be keeping
our eyes peeled for all the latest rumors

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:49.540
and leaks.

